/-!
# Finite data for the two-cell case of period-4 absorption

`sdata p φ = (t, k, j0)` is the single-cell witness for position `p`, phase `φ`: the
single-cell orbit is in the family at time `t` with run length `k` and alignment `j0`.
`dataAll p φ` lists, for the second cell at `q = p+1, p+2, …`, the first family time with
its run length and alignment.  `checkAll` verifies every entry against the packed
recurrence, and `checkSingleAll` verifies the single-cell witnesses.  These are finite
computations only; the mathematical reduction is in `Rule30EtherTwoCell`.
-/

